[{:name "reject-thin-dispatch-packets-before-agency-invoke"
  :level :loop
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:marker-kind :misdispatch
   :observation
   "The cohort-2 S1 register records that a one-line stub reached an Agency invoke because an echo-style dispatch did not preserve the intended multiline packet. The job received no repository, validation command, deliverable contract, or final-summary requirement."
   :proposed-rule
   "`dispatch_with_recall` should reject implausibly short stdin or packets missing required contract fields before invoking Agency, unless the operator explicitly supplies `--allow-thin`."
   :required-fields
   ["repository or working directory"
    "task/deliverable"
    "validation or acceptance criterion"
    "completion/reporting instruction"]
   :expected-effect
   "Turn a silent shell-packet truncation into an immediate, typed dispatch error instead of spending an agent job on an unactionable prompt."}
  :subjects
  [#:ref{:type :mission, :id "M-zai-learning-loop"}
   #:ref{:type :loop-component, :id "dispatch_with_recall"}]
  :evidence
  {:turn-round-ids []
   :commits []
   :problems ["lib-young"]
   :register-markers ["⊸fix [misdispatch]"]
   :jobs ["invoke-1785131793242-174"]}
  :confidence :single-instance
  :rationale
  "The typed operations register makes the cause and missing packet fields deterministic; a pre-invoke structural check is cheaper and more reliable than detecting the failure from the resulting session."
  :review {:verdict :pending-loop-review}}

